{
  "@context": "https://www.w3.org/2022/wot/td/v1.1",
  "@type": "tm:ThingModel",
  "title": "Issue",
  "titles": {
    "en": "Issue",
    "ru": "Беда"
  },
  "description": "Created by akt-priority as issue-<n>; safety_class S0, S1 or empty. loss_usd_h is the rate once losses run, loss_from the model minute they start (-1: none expected, or a safety issue that is not counted in money). status_ru: the status in Russian words; person: the person twin to call. eta: expected arrival of the called person or crew; escalation: 'not arrived by ETA + 15 min' text (empty when none). evidence = measurements behind the issue {items: [{label, thing, feature, text, unit, where, age_pub_min, age_meas_min, suspect, old}]}: age_pub_min is the age of the data on the screen, age_meas_min the age of the sample itself (analyser, grab sample); notify_text: roles told besides the one called (new face, regime to change). lifecycle = {stage, stage_ru, steps: [{key, ru, t, src}], help, help_text, text}: new, called, accepted, on the way, on site, resolved; accepted / on the way / on site come from the called person (journal.mech), else from the model, marked in src. lever = {name, line, value, unit, reason, label} (only for advice that changes the regime: the interface offers one click that sets this what-if lever in the model; empty otherwise). cost = {usd_h, items: [{key, title, usd_h, label, supports: [{what, label}]}], horizon, weakest, text}: the price split into copper, energy, reagents and penalty, and what each part stands on (fact, calculation, assumption). States: OPEN, CALLED, IN_WORK, RESOLVED, SNOOZED.",
  "version": {
    "model": "1.0.0"
  },
